  "id": "culpability",
  "term": "culpability",
  "definition": "Culpability is the state of deserving moral blame for a wrong act. It differs from legal responsibility because a person may be legally responsible without being morally blameworthy, and moral culpability depends on the person having done the act with knowledge, or with the ability to have known, what they were doing.",
